<title>What's Next With The ISFDB</title>
<h1>What's Next With The ISFDB</h1>
<hr>

This is just a list of upcoming attractions - it is non-binding,
not necessarily listed in any particular order, and scheduled for
whenever we get around to them. Updated: 24 Mar 97.

<ol>
 <li> Fix sorting routines to take 8-bit characters into account.
 <li> Finish research/cleanup associated with integrating the collections
      from the NESFA database; send error report back to NESFA.
 <li> Finish work begun on the Michael J. Cross collection database.
 <li> Begin work on the anthologies present in the NESFA database.
 <li> Update the FAQ page-by-page.
 <li> Fix [Alpha] option so that *all* titles are sorted, including
      those under pseudonyms.
 <li> Fix correction page for an existing anth/coll, such that
      it allows story entries to be made.
 <li> Fix magazine listings such that novels can be displayed. (easy)
 <li> Fix magazine listings such that awards can be displayed. (medium)
 <li> Add support for series notes. (medium/hard)
 <li> Add support such that publication data for serials shows up under
      the novel instead of on the author's summary bibliography. (hard)
 <li> A home version of the ISFDB which runs on Windows95 platforms is in
      the works. So far, a command-line version is up and running, which 
      means it would work on a Windows95 web server. It still needs to be 
      integrated with a browser-like user interface.
</ol>

